c1_colour_chart_session2.png  the chart printed in colour session 2 (from tools/make_colour_chart.py
                              before its width fix). It is 1440 px wide but its patch grid needs
                              1470, so every row crossing the last patch column is 36 bytes too
                              long: not a valid PNG. Windows printed it anyway, reading fixed
                              4321-byte rows, so the chart came out sheared (12 px per long row)
                              and each wrap shifted the RGB byte order. xtask::read_chart_png
                              reproduces that decode exactly; 145 of the 729 cube colours never
                              reached the page and are inferred by the fit.
c1_colour_chart.layout.json   patch list (colours, kinds) of that chart; positions are not used.
701_chart_matte_speed.prn     Windows capture of the chart, defaults (Matte, Speed, Preferred).
